From eba3c893e4132649650c65c74b444220a1d0fdc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:00:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add planRoute to stitch route legs (issue 3)

Getting a user back on track took two calculatePath calls and two
Instructions objects with nothing to join them.

- planRoute(tree, from, waypoints, options) plans each leg from the end of
  the previous one and returns one combined Path and one Instructions.
  Waypoints are { screen } or { action, repeat? }; repeat is a whole number
  or a $VAR$ from the route variables and stays data on the step.
- A leg that cannot be planned returns { ok: false, leg, error } (0-based).
  Unknown screens count, since the app's idea of the user's screen can be
  stale. Bad waypoint shapes throw INVALID_WAYPOINT.
- Path.legs, step.leg and Instructions.legs keep the leg boundaries.
  buildInstructions takes the combined path with no special casing.
- planRouteAsync for async extensions.
- The recovery example now uses planRoute. Tests, README, llms.txt,
  AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG.
